This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.

Summary:
1. Primary Request and Intent:
   The user's sole instruction (from the initial human turn) was: "Build the cinema seat-booking web application described in spec/README.md, as the Angular application already set up in this Nx workspace (Nx project `cinescope` in apps/cinescope); its stack is described in spec/stack.md. The work is split into tickets in spec/tickets/; implement them in order. spec/README.md is the complete specification: do not ask any questions, and where it is silent choose the simplest option that satisfies it. Finish only when every ticket is done and `pnpm nx build cinescope` succeeds."
   No further user messages followed; I have been autonomously implementing the full spec since then. Key constraints from spec/README.md that must be honored throughout: use pnpm only; do not change port 4200; do not add dependencies; do not hand-edit db.json; desktop-only viewport; all text in English; use the Angular Material UI library specifically for every button, text field, checkbox, toast, and the datepicker (seat map/legend/selected-seats panel are hand-drawn); exact `data-testid` contract in section 9 must be followed verbatim (no renaming/abbreviating/prefixing, and these testids must not appear on any other element); booking lifecycle and route guard rules in section 3.1; out-of-scope items explicitly excluded (user accounts, real payments, seat locking, updating occupiedSeats, images, responsive/mobile layouts, keyboard nav/ARIA beyond defaults, translations).

2. Key Technical Concepts:
   - Nx 23 monorepo, Angular 22.0.8 standalone components (standalone is default, no explicit flag needed), **zoneless** change detection (no zone.js installed; required explicit `provideZonelessChangeDetection()`).
   - Angular Material 22.0.7 + CDK — notably **no `@angular/animations` package is installed at all** (Material 22 no longer depends on it), so no animations provider is needed or possible.
   - Angular's new control-flow template syntax (`@if`, `@for`, `@switch`/`@case`) used throughout, including discriminated-union narrowing inside `@switch(cell.kind) { @case('seat') {...} }`.
   - `toSignal()` from `@angular/core/rxjs-interop` to bridge Router observables (`queryParamMap`, `paramMap`) into signals.
   - Angular signals (`signal`, `computed`, `effect`) as the primary reactivity model; `BookingService` is a signal-backed singleton synced to `sessionStorage`.
   - Reactive Forms (`NonNullableFormBuilder`, custom cross-field validators) confirmed compatible with zoneless Angular because Angular schedules change detection after any DOM event handled via Angular's event system/Renderer2 listeners (including those registered by `ControlValueAccessor` directives for blur/input), not just through signals.
   - `MatSnackBar.openFromComponent()` used for toast via `MAT_SNACK_BAR_DATA` injection token, satisfying "only one toast visible, replaces current, 4000ms auto-dismiss" requirement natively.
   - CSS Grid-based auditorium layout using fixed track widths and `grid-column: span N` for couches/entrance gaps.
   - Functional route guards (`CanActivateFn`) reading a synchronous signal from `BookingService`.
   - Lazy-loaded standalone routes via `loadComponent`.
   - `json-server` 0.17.4 backend serving `db.json` at `http://localhost:3000`; app calls it directly (CORS enabled).
   - pnpm package manager; `CI=true` env var needed to bypass an interactive TTY prompt during `pnpm nx build` when Nx auto-triggers `pnpm install`.

3. Files and Code Sections:

   - **`apps/cinescope/src/app/app.config.ts`** (edited) — Added zoneless CD and HTTP client providers:
     ```ts
     import { ApplicationConfig, provideBrowserGlobalErrorListeners, provideZonelessChangeDetection } from '@angular/core';
     import { provideHttpClient } from '@angular/common/http';
     import { provideNativeDateAdapter } from '@angular/material/core';
     import { provideRouter } from '@angular/router';
     import { appRoutes } from './app.routes';

     export const appConfig: ApplicationConfig = {
       providers: [
         provideBrowserGlobalErrorListeners(),
         provideZonelessChangeDetection(),
         provideRouter(appRoutes),
         provideHttpClient(),
         provideNativeDateAdapter(),
       ],
     };
     ```

   - **`apps/cinescope/src/app/app.routes.ts`** (rewritten) — Lazy routes + guards:
     ```ts
     import { Route } from '@angular/router';
     import { bookingInProgressGuard } from './core/guards/booking-in-progress.guard';
     import { paidBookingGuard } from './core/guards/paid-booking.guard';

     export const appRoutes: Route[] = [
       { path: '', loadComponent: () => import('./pages/movie-list/movie-list.component').then((m) => m.MovieListComponent) },
       { path: 'screenings/:id/seats', loadComponent: () => import('./pages/seat-map/seat-map.component').then((m) => m.SeatMapComponent) },
       { path: 'screenings/:id/summary', canActivate: [bookingInProgressGuard], loadComponent: () => import('./pages/summary/summary.component').then((m) => m.SummaryComponent) },
       { path: 'screenings/:id/checkout', canActivate: [bookingInProgressGuard], loadComponent: () => import('./pages/checkout/checkout.component').then((m) => m.CheckoutComponent) },
       { path: 'confirmation', canActivate: [paidBookingGuard], loadComponent: () => import('./pages/confirmation/confirmation.component').then((m) => m.ConfirmationComponent) },
       { path: '**', redirectTo: '' },
     ];
     ```

   - **Models** (`core/models/`):
     - `movie.model.ts` — `Movie { id, title, genre, runtimeMinutes, format: 'PL dubbing' | 'PL subtitles' }`.
     - `screening.model.ts` — `Screening { id, movieId, date, time, occupiedSeats: string[] }`.
     - `reservation.model.ts` — `ReservationCustomer`, `ReservationRequest`, `Reservation extends ReservationRequest { id }`.
     - `booking.model.ts`:
       ```ts
       export interface CheckoutFormValues {
         firstName: string; lastName: string; email: string; confirmEmail: string; phone: string; termsAccepted: boolean;
       }
       export interface Booking {
         screeningId: number; seats: string[]; paid: boolean; email: string | null; form: CheckoutFormValues;
       }
       export function emptyCheckoutForm(): CheckoutFormValues { ... }
       export function createBooking(screeningId: number): Booking { ... }
       ```

   - **`shared/date-utils.ts`** — `formatIsoDate`, `todayIso`, `parseIsoDate`, `addDaysIso`, `isValidIsoDate` (type-guard regex `^\d{4}-\d{2}-\d{2}$` plus round-trip check for invalid calendar dates), `normalizeDate(raw)` (defaults to today if missing/invalid/past, using lexicographic ISO string comparison), `weekdayName`, `formatShowDate(iso, time)` → e.g. `"Tuesday 15 Sep 16:00"`, `buildDayButtons(today)` → `[{label:'Today',date:today}, ...next 4 weekdays]` (IMPORTANT: computed from the real `todayIso()`, not from the currently selected date).

   - **`shared/seat-pricing.ts`** — `priceForRow(row)` (≤5→25, ≤10→32, ≤14→39, else 89), `formatPrice(amount)` → `"25.00 PLN"`.

   - **`shared/seat-grouping.ts`** — `parseSeatId(id)` (regex `^R(\d+)C(\d+)$`), `SeatGroup` interface `{ row, kind:'seat'|'couch', column, columnStart, columnEnd, price, ids: string[] }`, `groupSeats(ids)` (groups by row ascending, sorts columns ascending, pairs row-15 ids two-at-a-time into couches), `sortSeatsForSummary(ids)` (sort by row then column, used for POST payload), `totalPrice(ids)`.

   - **`shared/auditorium.ts`** — Types `SeatState = 'available'|'selected'|'unavailable'|'accessible'`, `SeatCell`, `CouchCell`, `AisleCell`, `EmptyCell`, `AuditoriumCell`, `AuditoriumRow`. `seatId(row,col)`, `seatCell(row,col)` (accessible = row===1 && col 10-15), `couchCell(row,columnStart)`. `leftBlock(row)` (row15→2 couches; row≤10→`[{kind:'empty'}]`; else 4 seats), `middleBlock(row)` (row15→8 couches cols5-19 step2; else cols5-20 seats), `rightBlock(row)` (row15→2 couches 21-22/23-24; else cols21-24 seats). `buildAuditorium()` assembles 15 rows as `[...leftBlock, {kind:'aisle'}, ...middleBlock, {kind:'aisle'}, ...rightBlock]`. `cellIds(cell)` returns `[cell.id]` or `cell.ids`. `stateOf(ids, accessible, occupied, selected)` returns unavailable/selected/accessible/available per spec priority.

   - **`shared/seat-colors.ts`** — `SEAT_COLORS: Record<SeatState,string>` with exact hex values from spec (`#2E7D32`, `#F9A825`, `#C62828`, `#1565C0`); `LEGEND_ITEMS` array of `{state, label}` in spec order (Available, Selected, Unavailable, Accessible).

   - **`shared/toast/toast.component.ts`**:
     ```ts
     @Component({ selector: 'app-toast', template: `<span data-testid="toast">{{ data.message }}</span>` })
     export class ToastComponent {
       protected readonly data = inject<ToastData>(MAT_SNACK_BAR_DATA);
     }
     ```

   - **`core/services/toast.service.ts`** — `ToastService.show(message)` calls `snackBar.openFromComponent(ToastComponent, { data:{message}, duration:4000, horizontalPosition:'center', verticalPosition:'bottom' })`.

   - **`core/services/movies.service.ts`** — `getMovies()`, `getMovie(id)`, `getScreeningsByDate(date)` (uses `params:{date}`), `getScreening(id)`. Base URL `http://localhost:3000`.

   - **`core/services/reservations.service.ts`** — `createReservation(payload: ReservationRequest): Observable<Reservation>` via POST.

   - **`core/services/booking.service.ts`** — Full implementation:
     ```ts
     const STORAGE_KEY = 'cinescope:booking';
     export type ToggleResult = 'selected' | 'deselected' | 'limit';
     const MAX_SEATS = 10;

     @Injectable({ providedIn: 'root' })
     export class BookingService {
       private readonly state = signal<Booking | null>(readFromStorage());
       readonly booking = this.state.asReadonly();

       startNewBooking(screeningId: number): void { this.persist(createBooking(screeningId)); }
       ensureBookingForScreening(screeningId: number): void {
         const current = this.state();
         if (!current || current.paid || current.screeningId !== screeningId) this.startNewBooking(screeningId);
       }
       clearBooking(): void { this.persist(null); }
       toggleSeats(ids: string[]): ToggleResult { /* dedup/limit logic as described */ }
       removeSeats(ids: string[]): void { ... }
       updateForm(form: CheckoutFormValues): void { ... }
       markPaid(email: string): void { ... }
       private persist(booking: Booking | null): void { sets signal + sessionStorage.setItem/removeItem }
     }
     function readFromStorage(): Booking | null { try/catch JSON.parse from sessionStorage }
     ```

   - **`core/guards/booking-in-progress.guard.ts`** and **`paid-booking.guard.ts`** — functional `CanActivateFn`s reading `BookingService.booking()` synchronously and `router.parseUrl('/')` as fallback.

   - **`pages/movie-list/movie-list.component.ts` + `.html` + `.scss`** — Day picker (five `day-button`s + Material datepicker with `min` bound to today, `data-date`/`data-selected` attrs) and movie list with `status` signal (`'loading'|'error'|'loaded'`), `movies` signal of `MovieCard[]` (Movie + sorted screenings for that date), `effect()` reloading on `selectedDate()` change, `retry()`, `selectDate(date)` (router.navigate with queryParamsHandling:'merge'), `openScreening(id)`. Template uses `@switch(status())` for loading/error/loaded states and nested `@for`/`@if` for movie-list/movies-empty. All section 9.1 testids present.

   - **`pages/seat-map/seat-map.component.ts` + `.html` + `.scss`** — Loads screening via `MoviesService.getScreening(id)` inside an `effect()` keyed on route id signal; on success calls `bookingService.ensureBookingForScreening(id)` then sets `screening`/`loaded` signals; on error navigates to `/`. Computed signals: `occupiedSet`, `selectedSet`, `selectedCount`, `selectedGroups` (via `groupSeats`), `selectedRows`, `subtitle` (`Show Date: ${formatShowDate(...)}`). Methods: `seatColor(state)`, `cellState(ids,accessible)` (delegates to `stateOf`), **`idsFor(cell)`** (renamed from an original naming collision — see Errors section), `onSeatClick(ids,state)` (ignores unavailable; shows toast `'Maximum 10 seats per booking'` on limit), `rowGroupLine(row)`, `cancel()` (clearBooking + navigate '/'), `continue()` (no-op if 0 selected, else navigate to summary). Template renders title/subtitle/seat-limit-info/screen-indicator/seat-map grid (rows with row-label-left/right, aisle, seat, couch cells via `@switch(cell.kind)`)/legend/selected-seats panel/cancel+continue buttons, all with exact data-testid attributes from spec section 9.2.

   - **`pages/summary/summary.component.ts` + `.html` + `.scss`** — Loads screening then movie sequentially (nested subscribes), redirects to `/` on either failure or NaN id. `items` computed via `groupSeats`, `total` computed as sum of prices. `seatLabel(item)` → `Couch a-b` or column number. `remove(item)` removes ids from booking; if `seats.length===0` after removal, navigates to seat map. `back()`/`confirm()` navigate accordingly. Template uses exact data-testids from section 9.3; `summary-total` text is `Total: {{ formatPrice(total()) }}`.

   - **`pages/checkout/checkout.component.ts` + `.html` + `.scss`** — Uses `NonNullableFormBuilder`. Custom validators `emailFormatValidator` (regex `/^[^\s@]+@[^\s@]+\.[^\s@]+$/`) and `confirmEmailValidator` (compares to sibling `email` control's current value via `control.parent`). Form group fields: firstName/lastName (`required`+`minLength(2)`), email (`required`+custom), confirmEmail (`required`+custom), phone (`Validators.pattern(/^\d{9}$/)` only, no required), termsAccepted (`Validators.requiredTrue`). Constructor patches form from `bookingService.booking()?.form` without marking touched, subscribes to `valueChanges` to persist to `BookingService.updateForm`, and subscribes to `email.valueChanges` to re-trigger confirmEmail validity (`updateValueAndValidity({onlySelf:true, emitEvent:false})`). `fieldError(name, requiredMessage, errorKey, errorMessage)` helper returns null unless `control.touched`, else required-message-first-else-specific-message logic. `touchTerms()` manually marks termsAccepted touched on `(change)`. `pay()`: if invalid → `markAllAsTouched()` + toast `'The form contains errors'`, no request; if valid → builds `ReservationRequest` with `sortSeatsForSummary(booking.seats)`, submits via `ReservationsService`, toggles `submitting` signal, on success calls `bookingService.markPaid(value.email)` then navigates to `/confirmation`, on error shows toast `'Payment failed. Please try again.'`. Template renders all 6 fields with exact labels (`First name *`, etc., phone label without asterisk), error divs conditionally shown via `@if(fieldError(...); as message)`, terms checkbox via `mat-checkbox`, Back/Pay buttons with pay button text `Pay ${formatPrice(total())}` or `'Processing…'` while submitting, `[disabled]="submitting()"`.

   - **`pages/confirmation/confirmation.component.ts` + `.html` + `.scss`** — `email` computed from `bookingService.booking()?.email`, `continue()` clears booking and navigates to `/`. Template has exact section 9.5 testids.

4. Errors and fixes:
   - **Naming collision** in `seat-map.component.ts`: I initially defined a component method `cellIds(cell)` with the same name as the imported pure function `cellIds` from `shared/auditorium.ts`. Although this would technically still resolve correctly via JS/TS lexical scoping (bare identifier inside the method body refers to the module-level import, not `this.cellIds`), it was confusing and risky style. **Fix**: renamed the component method to `idsFor` via `Edit` tool (`cellIds(cell: Parameters<typeof cellIds>[0]): string[] { return cellIds(cell); }` → `idsFor(cell: Parameters<typeof cellIds>[0]): string[] { return cellIds(cell); }`), then used `sed -i 's/cellIds(cell)/idsFor(cell)/g'` on `seat-map.component.html` to update all 6 template usages, and verified via grep that all occurrences changed correctly.
